    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d384">

                <pb facs="0544" n="448" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg448"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/25070</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Navy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Denby</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-07-02"><hi rendition="#italic">July 2,
                        1921</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I am in receipt of your
                    letter of July 1st<anchor n="63" xml:id="d384-f1"/> acquainting me with the
                    situation at Tampico. The Department has ordered the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sacramento</hi> from Galveston to proceed immediately <pb facs="0545"
                        n="449" xml:id="pg449"/> to Tampico where she should arrive on Monday.
                    Another ship has been ordered up from the Canal Zone and I hope the force
                    present will be sufficient to prevent any trouble.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin Denby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
